139:Cor. 4.9 (`xu-layout.txt:336-339`), not a general skeleton equality.
140:
141:## 3. Same-tree identity for the `I` constraint
142:
143:Let
144:
145:```text
146:W_T = sum_{sigma in P_m} (|D_sigma^{f_xi}|-1)(delta_sigma-1).
147:```
148:
149:Xu's equation (4.3) on p.6 gives, on the same tree,
150:
151:```text
152:I(f_xi, f_y g) = deg_y f + sum_{sigma in P_m}|D_sigma^{f_xi}|(delta_sigma-1)
153:               = deg_y f + W_T + (Im_T - 1).
154:```
155:
156:Using `I(f_xi,f_y g)=I_T+I(f_xi,g)` and Theorem 5.1,
157:
158:```text
159:I_T + IM_T = deg_y f + W_T + Im_T - 1.
160:```
161:
162:Therefore
163:
164:```text
165:deg_y f - 1 + W_T - I_T = IM_T - Im_T.              (*)
166:```
167:
168:So once the test is same-tree, Theorem 3.4's exact `I_T` plus Theorem 4.7(i)
169:is not a second inequality.  Its slack is exactly the Corollary 5.3 slack.
170:The driver records the two slacks equal; `audit_sametree.py` asserts equality
171:on all 1420 rows.  This is the cheapest safe use of Theorem 3.4 under
172:`FALLACY-v2`: do not invent an unproved skeleton target for `I_T`.
173:
174:## 4. Implementation
175:
176:`xu_sametree.py` imports the frozen lane inputs, not mutable workspace copies
177:(`xu_sametree.py:35-40`).  The operative row set is exactly the charged
178:`C_FULL_TREE_POLYNOMIAL_ODE` set: `M.census(... full=True)` filtered by
179:`FT.full_tree_polynomial_ode_ok` (`xu_sametree.py:799-812`).
180:
181:The finite tree model is the charged model: the selected Moh `V` path must
182:embed, major children recurse, terminal minor packets contribute their
183:first final order, polynomial-recentering danger and ODE nondegeneracy are
184:on (`xu_sametree.py:2-19`, `227-252`, `319-322`).
185:
186:Per-terminal metrics:
187:
188:* Principal packet: roots `u_s m/d_s`, order `V_s/u_s`, contribution
189:  `V_s/u_s-1`, weighted contribution `(u_s m/d_s - 1)(V_s/u_s-1)`, and
190:  `I` contribution `(u_s m/d_s)(V_s/u_s)` (`xu_sametree.py:244-252`).
191:* Nonprincipal terminal minor packet: `delta=S_out/N`, checked against the
192:  charged formula
193:  `delta_j + (d_j/(n-M_j))(1-delta_j)/v`; its `Im`, weighted, and `I`
194:  contributions are computed exactly inside the finite terminal-packet model
195:  (`xu_sametree.py:260-286`).
196:* Bottom major packet: `(12)/(13)` is checked before contributing; the
197:  distance identity for `S(alpha)` is asserted before adding `IM`
198:  (`xu_sametree.py:288-317`).
199:
200:The same-tree optimisation is a scalar DP over `IM-Im`: `DIFF_MAX` adds
201:major `IM` contributions and subtracts minor `Im` contributions on the same
202:completion.  The selected-zero and selected-nonzero embedding cases follow
203:the charged driver, with cached multiset optimisation rather than
204:materialising all partitions (`xu_sametree.py:383-504`, `552-588`).  The
205:independent extrema are computed by the same scalar engine in `IM_MAX` and
206:`IM_MIN` modes; `candidate_compare.log` verifies row-level equality with the
207:frozen `xu_screen_candidate.py` bounder.
